{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Set rules for MPs' social media use in the Code of Conduct",
        "additional_details": "Political commentary from MPs on social media is currently not covered by the Code of Conduct, unless it causes \u201csignificant damage\u201d to the reputation of the House or MPs generally. We believe this means MPs are able to use divisive language, stigmatizing entire communities, without parliamentary oversight. MPs should adhere to standards of accuracy, dignity and responsibility online.",
        "background": "Update the Code of Conduct for MPs so it covers MPs' social media use, establishing clear rules against using any inflammatory rhetoric or dehumanizing language, including associating national or ethnic symbols with gangs.",
